Q: Extract Matrix of Values from Matrix using Matrix of Row Numbers A: <p>You <em>could</em> also preallocate the resulting matrix and assign with <code>[] &lt;-</code> :</p>
<pre><code>res2 &lt;- matrix(NA_character_, nrow = n_rows_out, ncol = n_cols)
res2[] &lt;- vals[val_rows, val_col]
res2

#      [,1]  [,2]  [,3] 
# [1,] &quot;3x2&quot; &quot;4x2&quot; &quot;3x2&quot;
# [2,] &quot;1x2&quot; &quot;3x2&quot; &quot;5x2&quot;
# [3,] &quot;3x2&quot; &quot;4x2&quot; &quot;2x2&quot;
# [4,] &quot;1x2&quot; &quot;5x2&quot; &quot;5x2&quot;
</code></pre>

Q: &quot;Illegal string offset&quot; error while executing raw INSERT queries in a loop with CodeIgniter A: <pre><code>    type = '" . $this-&gt;db-&gt;escape($option['type']) . "'");
}
</code></pre>

<p><code>$option['type']</code> at the end there should be <code>$option_type['type']</code> - <code>$option</code> is from your outer foreach loop, and contains one of your integers from <code>$data['options']</code> at this point. </p>

Q: How can I force trailing zero in a numeric format string? A: <p>Let's say you had a variable called &quot;myNumber&quot; of type double:</p>
<pre><code>double myNumber = 1520;
</code></pre>
<p>Instead of:</p>
<pre><code>myNumber.ToString(&quot;N2&quot;); // returns &quot;1,520.00&quot;
</code></pre>
<p>I would opt for:</p>
<pre><code>myNumber.ToString(&quot;0.00&quot;); // returns &quot;1520.00&quot;
</code></pre>
<p>since N2 will add &quot;,&quot; thousands separators, which can often cause problems downstream.</p>
